        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1087,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1072,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 1088,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152423,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1088,
        "headingText": "<font color=\"red\">Classification in progress, Data not available in this Beta</font>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1073,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 1089,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152424,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1089,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> atypical proliferative Brenner tumour.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1074,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 1090,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152425,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1090,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1075,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1091,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152426,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1091,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are unilateral and confined to the ovary {22954784; 30779594; 33768396}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1076,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1092,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152427,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1092,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients often present with a pelvic mass {22954784; 30779594}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1077,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1093,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152428,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1093,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>This is a very uncommon tumour, representing &lt;&nbsp;0.5&ndash;2.8% of epithelial ovarian neoplasms in case series. Patients are usually &gt;&nbsp;50&nbsp;years old {22954784; 38539441; 35000896}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1078,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1094,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152429,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1094,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>These tumours are presumed to arise from benign Brenner tumours.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1079,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1095,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152430,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1095,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Disease-specific mutations are not known. Homozygous deletion of <em>CDKN2A</em> (the gene encoding p16INK4a) have been reported, resulting in loss of p16 staining by immunohistochemistry {23887305; 32322877}. Mutations may be present in <em>KRAS</em> and <em>PIK3CA</em> {23887305; 19033864}, but not in <em>TP53</em> {28639280; 19033864}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1086,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1102,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152431,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1102,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unlike benign Brenner tumours, borderline Brenner tumours are typically large (median size: 120&nbsp;mm) and cystic {22954784}. Papillary masses project into the cyst lumen. Solid areas often reflect a benign Brenner component. Rarely, the tumour is completely solid.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1080,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1096,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152432,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1096,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most of these tumours resemble low-grade papillary urothelial neoplasms of the urothelial tract. The cytological features can vary, but the cells are usually uniform and show elongated nuclei with fine chromatin and visible nucleoli; occasionally, moderate to severe cytological atypia is present {26837300; 38733672}. Mucinous or squamous metaplasia is often found. Areas of benign Brenner tumour are nearly always present. An uncommon pattern is one with marked crowding of the nests of urothelial-type epithelium, which may be large and tortuous. Although there is increased mitotic activity and/or cytological atypia in these lesions, there should be no evidence of stromal invasion.</p>\r\n<h5><em>Immunohistochemistry</em></h5>\r\n<p>Immunohistochemistry is usually positive for p63 and GATA3 and negative for ER, PR, and WT1 {19033864; 19092634; 17880529; 14576476}. p53 shows a wildtype immunoreactive pattern, and p16 can show loss of staining {23887305; 32322877}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1081,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1097,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152433,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1097,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1082,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1098,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152434,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1098,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1085,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1101,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152435,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1101,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential: </em>papillary growth resembling low-grade urothelial neoplasms of the urothelial tract, without stromal invasion.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> a benign Brenner component.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1083,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1099,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152436,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1099,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Borderline Brenner tumour is staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em> [[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM Classification of Malignant Tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]) and the FIGO staging system.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1084,
    "bookid": 85,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1100,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 152437,
        "bookId": 85,
        "chapterId": 141,
        "headingId": 1100,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The behaviour is usually benign; local recurrence is rare {22954784; 5074634; 30779594}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-25T19:23:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]